WEBVTT

NOTE
Captions for the bundled sample lesson video (/media/lesson-sample.mp4).
Generated with it by scripts/make-lesson-video.mjs — edit the slide script
there, not this file. Served from the client bundle, so no request leaves
the origin. Replace per-lesson by setting `captionsUrl`.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Welcome back. In this lesson we define one schema per request body.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.500
We infer the TypeScript type from that schema, so there is a single
source of truth for both validation and types.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:36.000
Then we return structured 422 errors the frontend can map onto fields.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:26.000
The schema lives in the shared package, so the client and the server
read the same rules.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:51.000
The type is inferred, so a hand-written interface can never drift from it.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:16.000
One middleware parses the body, so a controller only ever sees data
that has already passed.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:41.000
Errors come back keyed by field name, which is what a form needs.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:06.000
The client sets each field error it is handed, and keeps no rules of its own.

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:31.000
Browser validation is a courtesy. The server check is the one that counts.

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:56.000
That means a validation rule is written once and enforced everywhere.

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:25.000
Next: moving the rules out of the controller and into a service layer.
